This project is an independent ZCode & Antigravity implementation inspired by:

- pstack, https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
  Copyright Cursor, MIT License. Original skill set, verification maintenance
  model, and code-as-comments ("no-comments") discipline by Lauren Tan.
- cursor-team-kit & cli-for-agent, https://github.com/cursor/plugins
  Copyright Cursor, MIT License. CLI/TUI verification harnesses (control-cli),
  three-way claim verdicts (verify-this), agent-friendly CLI conventions
  (cli-for-agents), and redundant-code cleanup (deslop).
- open-pstack, https://github.com/ericlitman/open-pstack
  Copyright Eric Litman, MIT License. Verification-skill architecture and the
  exact-head evidence model.
- ponytail, https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail
  Copyright Dietrich Gebert, MIT License. The necessity ladder, the
  over-engineering review rubric, the audit report structure, and the
  "shortcut:" comment convention used by kelin-refine and kelin-audit.
- impeccable (Apache License 2.0) is an optional external UI skill. kelin-ui
  delegates to it when it is installed and ships its own checklist otherwise.
  No impeccable code or text is copied into this repository.

No upstream source file is copied verbatim. The skill text, scripts, tests and
verification harness in this repository were written for ZCode and Antigravity
in Chinese. Shared ideas: the plan/verify/review/ship workflow split, the
"proof over claims" verification stance, the feature-map plus recipe structure
used by the verifier, and the minimal-code ladder adapted for kelin-refine.
